\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Nonlinearity enables complex decision boundaries. (a) An XOR-like classification problem: no straight line separates the classes. (b) A single hidden layer creates a piecewise-linear boundary. (c) A deeper network produces a smooth boundary that perfectly separates the data.}}{4}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:decision_boundary}{{3}{4}{Nonlinearity enables complex decision boundaries. (a) An XOR-like classification problem: no straight line separates the classes. (b) A single hidden layer creates a piecewise-linear boundary. (c) A deeper network produces a smooth boundary that perfectly separates the data}{figure.3}{}}
